# This machine has `core.autocrlf=true`, and without this file git applied
# line-ending conversion to four QA screenshots on their way into a commit —
# stripping CR bytes from inside the PNG payload, so the stored blob was several
# hundred bytes shorter than the file on disk and no longer a decodable image.
# Git's own text/binary heuristic had not protected them.
#
# `text=auto` keeps the normal LF-in-the-repo behaviour for source, and every
# format below is declared binary so its bytes are stored exactly as they are.
# `eol=lf` also checks text out as LF on every OS: with `core.autocrlf=true`
# a Windows checkout was CRLF, and `prettier --check` (LF) failed on a clean clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.svgz binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.db binary
